# Both images build with the repo root as context (docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: ../..`), so without this file every build ships ~1.5 GB to the
# daemon, most of it host-built virtualenvs and node_modules.
#
# This is a deny list, not an allow list: the Dockerfiles COPY named paths
# (packages, services, api, fixtures, knowledge, evaluations, web), so anything
# not listed here still reaches the build. Adding a path the Dockerfiles COPY
# will break the build rather than slim it.

# Host-built environments. Dockerfile runs `uv sync` and Dockerfile.web runs
# `npm ci` inside the image; copying the host's trees in is both wasted transfer
# and wrong, since Windows/macOS native binaries do not run on the Alpine and
# slim base images.
.venv/
venv/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
.next-dev/
.next-dev-*/

# Python build and cache artifacts.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-tmp-*/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/

# Version control and CI. Nothing in the images reads git history.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Secrets. These are gitignored too, but a stray .env in a working tree would
# otherwise be baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Local run artifacts and databases.
reports/
.evaluation_output/
*.log
.cloudcause/
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# Docs and infra: not imported by any service at runtime. The Dockerfile copies
# README.md explicitly, so it is re-included below.
docs/
docker/
terraform/
cloudbuild.yaml
*.md
!README.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.superdesign/
